  "progression": "The degree has 60 EC in each year and 157.5 EC of compulsory study. It begins with tissues, molecules, genomics and physiology before infection, circulation and blood. The second year develops digestion, kidneys, endocrinology, nutrition, skin, neurology, anaesthesia and welfare. Third-year reproductive, public-health, locomotor, epidemiological, multisystem and surgical work continues the clinical and professional sequences. The first-year study advice threshold is 45 EC subject to the stated exceptions. Active participation and course-specific practical attendance apply. Graduation requires passing the courses and the professional portfolio. The 10.5 EC third-year professional sequence includes the 7.5 EC thesis, supervised and marked by at least two examiners. Profiling courses provide 15 EC in year 2 period 4 and 7.5 EC in year 3 period 3. At least 7.5 EC must be outside the faculty, with academic level, approval and non-overlap rules. The OER also counts the thesis in its 30 EC description of profiling. It is counted only once in the 180 EC total.",
